1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,776
Why the fuck did one rock

2
00:00:01,796 --> 00:00:03,364
kill the dinosaurs?

3
00:00:03,680 --> 00:00:04,913
It wasn't the hit.

4
00:00:05,176 --> 00:00:06,570
It was the darkness.

5
00:00:07,022 --> 00:00:08,173
Here's how it works.

6
00:00:08,457 --> 00:00:10,429
66 million years ago,

7
00:00:10,449 --> 00:00:13,026
Tina the Triceratops is eating ferns.

8
00:00:13,252 --> 00:00:15,685
Then a rock about 10 km wide

9
00:00:15,705 --> 00:00:17,458
slams into Mexico at up to

10
00:00:17,478 --> 00:00:21,766
72,000 km/h. It leaves a crater about

11
00:00:21,786 --> 00:00:23,821
180 km wide.

12
00:00:24,221 --> 00:00:25,152
Step one:

13
00:00:25,257 --> 00:00:28,065
fire. Debris rains back down,

14
00:00:28,085 --> 00:00:29,248
the sky heats up,

15
00:00:29,268 --> 00:00:30,772
and forests burn.

16
00:00:31,213 --> 00:00:32,167
Step two:

17
00:00:32,390 --> 00:00:34,119
darkness. Soot,

18
00:00:34,140 --> 00:00:36,496
dust and sulfur block the sun.

19
00:00:36,726 --> 00:00:38,967
Plants get under 1% of normal

20
00:00:38,987 --> 00:00:40,591
light for over a year.

21
00:00:41,040 --> 00:00:42,018
Step three:

22
00:00:42,127 --> 00:00:44,406
starvation. No sun,

23
00:00:44,426 --> 00:00:45,431
no plants.

24
00:00:45,576 --> 00:00:45,948
No plants,

25
00:00:45,968 --> 00:00:46,580
no Tina.

26
00:00:46,600 --> 00:00:47,565
No Tina,

27
00:00:47,810 --> 00:00:48,731
no T. rex.

28
00:00:48,832 --> 00:00:50,067
About 75% of all species,

29
00:00:50,298 --> 00:00:53,051
gone. But there's one twist.

30
00:00:53,219 --> 00:00:53,887
Not every dinosaur died.

31
00:00:54,348 --> 00:00:56,120
Birds made it.

32
00:00:56,390 --> 00:00:59,042
Scientists think beaks let them eat

33
00:00:59,063 --> 00:01:02,714
seeds. Meanwhile,

34
00:01:03,015 --> 00:01:03,744
